{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792269439,"nonce":"CbTLd/89pWVuG+89E22jvDyzjYc=","title":"An element child inside markup in an array comprehension is drawn as the text of its class name","message":"**What**\n\nWith `--macro ashui.ui.Markup.enable()`, markup written inside a `for` comprehension in a child expression turns a child element into its type name as text. Found by RayDE building a workbench on ashui c3ff00d: `\u003ctabs\u003e{[for (f in files) \u003ctabs-content value={f}\u003e${editor(f)}\u003c/tabs-content\u003e]}\u003c/tabs\u003e`, where `editor(f)` returns a `\u003ccode-editor/\u003e` typed Element, shows the text \"ashui.components.CodeEditor\"; `{editor(f)}` in the same place did the same. Text children in the same position, such as tab labels, are fine. Moving the whole `\u003ctabs-content\u003e...\u003c/tabs-content\u003e` into a helper function that returns it, and writing `{[for (f in files) page(f)]}`, works, which RayDE does for now.\n\n**Reproducer, ashui alone**\n\n    static function item(f:String):Element return \u003ctext\u003eitem {f}\u003c/text\u003e;\n    var direct:Div = Owner.root(tree, _ -\u003e \u003cdiv\u003e{[for (f in files) \u003cdiv id={f}\u003e${item(f)}\u003c/div\u003e]}\u003c/div\u003e);\n    var wrapped:Div = Owner.root(tree, _ -\u003e \u003cdiv\u003e{[for (f in files) page(f)]}\u003c/div\u003e);   // page(f) returns \u003cdiv id={f}\u003e${item(f)}\u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe first draws each box's child as the text `ashui.ui.Text`; the second draws `item a` and `item b`. Both compiled against ashui 3d9c201 under Ash.\n\n**To find out**\n\nWhether the markup inside the comprehension reaches ashui's Markup lowering at all, or is left to tink_hxx's own, which stringifies an interpolated child. Compare how `\u003cfor\u003e` lowers the same body.","files":null}]}